<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<TcPlcObject Version="1.1.0.1">
  <POU Name="ATT_TO_IO" Id="{18b528b7-b147-4652-8142-65b2d820ca1f}" SpecialFunc="None">
    <Declaration><![CDATA[(*
ATT_TO_IO : convert an internal attenuator record to its EPICS-facing IO form.

Purpose:
    Copy ST_PMPS_Attenuator - the internal beam-parameter attenuator record -
    into the plain ST_PMPS_Attenuator_IO struct that crosses the IO boundary
    and is published to EPICS. ST_PMPS_Attenuator EXTENDS
    ST_PMPS_Attenuator_IO and adds only pytmc metadata (pv: Att with EGU %,
    pv: OK), so the conversion is a field-for-field copy of nTran and xAttOK
    with no scaling, clamping or interpretation applied along the way.

Usage:
    Called once per attenuator slot while a whole beam-parameter set is being
    published, from BP_TO_IO:

        BP_TO_IO.astAttenuators[idx] := ATT_TO_IO(BP.astAttenuators[idx]);

    A pure combinational helper: it holds no state, uses no timers, raises no
    fault and performs no validity check, so it is safe to call every scan.
    Deciding whether the transmission it reports is safe to publish is the
    caller's job (see F_AttenuatorOK and F_SafeBPCompare).

Objectives:
    - One place that names the attenuator field mapping between the internal
      record and the IO record, instead of each IO boundary copying by hand.
    - Keep the IO struct from drifting from the internal record: the two
      assignments mirror ST_PMPS_Attenuator_IO member-for-member.
    - Carry units across unchanged - the copy must never rescale.

Returns (ST_PMPS_Attenuator_IO) - each field is also commented where it is
assigned in the implementation:
    nTran : UINT - attenuator transmission, reported as a percentage value
            (pytmc declares EGU % on ST_PMPS_Attenuator). Copied unchanged,
            so no unit conversion happens here.
    xAttOK : UINT - attenuator health flag with boolean meaning: non-zero
            when the attenuator reports no errors and is stable, zero when
            it is not known-good (per ST_PMPS_Attenuator).

History:
    2020-05-21  Alex Wallace : Created - preparing for the addition of BP
                               elements; changed from nAtt to nTran when
                               PMPS switched to transmission (2020-07-07).
    2026-11-27  Scirix Agent : Header given purpose, usage, objectives and
                               the returned field contract, plus inline
                               comments on the input and the copied fields.
                               Comments only - no code change (audit
                               finding #391).
*)
FUNCTION ATT_TO_IO : ST_PMPS_Attenuator_IO
VAR_INPUT
    // Attenuator record to convert: the internal ST_PMPS_Attenuator, i.e.
    // ST_PMPS_Attenuator_IO plus the pytmc PV metadata. nTran carries the
    // transmission as a percentage value (EGU % as declared there) and xAttOK
    // the health flag (non-zero = no errors and stable; no units).
    Att : ST_PMPS_Attenuator;
END_VAR
VAR
END_VAR
]]></Declaration>
    <Implementation>
      <ST><![CDATA[ATT_TO_IO.nTran := Att.nTran; // Transmission in percent (EGU %); copied unchanged, never rescaled.
ATT_TO_IO.xAttOK := Att.xAttOK; // Health flag: non-zero = no errors and attenuator stable.]]></ST>
    </Implementation>
  </POU>
</TcPlcObject>